  "pages": [
    {
      "page_id": "p01",
      "text": "Hair grows out of a tiny pit in your skin: thin fair hair on your arms, thick hair on your head.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p01.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p01.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 8202,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p01.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 9639
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p02",
      "text": "One head can hold a hundred thousand hairs, and fair hair is the thinnest hair of all.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p02.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p02.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7314,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p02.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 7758
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p03",
      "text": "Your hair is dead, so a haircut in the barber chair does not hurt. Pull a hair and you yell!",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p03.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p03.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7470,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p03.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 10893
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p04",
      "text": "A round hair pit grows hair that hangs down. A flat hair pit grows hair with a curl.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p04.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p04.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7366,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p04.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8463
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p05",
      "text": "Head hair grows and grows, but arm hair and leg hair quit at a bit of fuzz. Lucky us!",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p05.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p05.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 8097,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p05.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8228
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p06",
      "text": "Eyebrows and eyelashes are hair. A pair of eyebrows stops sweat; a pair of eyelashes flicks dust out of the air.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p06.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p06.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 10422,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p06.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 11859
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p07",
      "text": "A lamb's hair is wool, and wool traps air. A pair of warm wool socks is just trapped air, not thick hair.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p07.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p07.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 10527,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p07.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 11206
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p08",
      "text": "Hair care is simple: wash your hair, brush your hair, and let the air dry your hair.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p08.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p08.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 7262,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p08.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 7915
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p09",
      "text": "Wet hair rips faster than dry hair, so a hairbrush is unfair to wet hair.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p09.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p09.mp3",
      "duration_ms": 6034,
      "voice": "57785406027844b29b63a772a8477bc2",
      "has_video": false,
      "song_audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/song/p09.mp3",
      "song_duration_ms": 8228
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p10",
      "text": "Hunt for hair: on the chair, on the stairs, in the hairbrush. You shed a hundred hairs a day and never miss one.",
      "image": "books/mlr_dec_076/pages/p10.webp",
      "audio": "books/mlr_dec_076/audio/pages/p10.mp3",
